⚽
"Letter Pile"/en
=== start
¶A giant serif U is the bucket. Five big letters tumble into it, then hearts
and soccer balls rain down and settle into their bowls and hooks. Everything
collides by the shape of its outline rather than by the rectangle around it,
which is what lets the U hold anything at all, a ball come to rest inside the
bowl of a letter instead of floating above it, and a heart wedge its point
between two letters.¶

¶The bucket is a letter like the rest, in a serif face so its arms end in
ledges. It needs a Motion to be solid, and so much mass that nothing landing
in it can push it around. It stands on the floor between two walls that just
touch its sides: its bottom is round, so without them it would rock over as
the pile grows.¶
cup: Phrase(
	'U'
	22m
	face: "Merriweather"
	name: "cup"
	place: Motion(Place(-8.1m -11m))
	color: Color(85% 10 250°)
	matter: Matter(mass: 5000kg friction: 0.9 outline: ⊤)
)

¶A heavy display face, because a fat letter has a bowl wide enough to catch a
ball. The letters are chosen for their hooks and bowls.¶
face: "Titan One"
letters: ['a' 'b' 'c' 'd' 'e']

¶The letters drop first, from the same place but staggered heights, so each one
lands on the last and the pile builds upward.

A letter is solid only because its place is a Motion and it has Matter — output
that a program places is a ghost that everything passes through. Their mass is
what keeps the balls from shoving the pile apart, and asking Matter for an
outline is what makes them collide by their letterforms.¶
pile: letters.translate(
	ƒ(letter•'' index•#)
		Phrase(
			letter
			3m
			face
			name: "letter\index\"
			place: Motion(
				Place(((index × 0.5m) - 2m) ((index × 5m) + 8m))
			)
			color: Color(75% 80 (index × 62°))
			matter: Matter(mass: 60kg friction: 0.9 outline: ⊤)
		)
)

¶The hearts fall next. An emoji can ask for its outline too, so each heart
collides by its shape: its point slips into the gaps a box would sit on top of.¶
hearts: ['🧡' '💛' '💚' '💙' '💜' '🩷'].translate(
	ƒ(heart•'' index•#)
		Phrase(
			heart
			2m
			name: "heart\index\"
			place: Motion(
				Place(((index × 0.6m) - 2.2m) ((index × 1.5m) + 34m))
			)
			matter: Matter(mass: 20kg friction: 0.8 outline: ⊤)
		)
)

¶The balls start above everything, so they arrive after the pile has settled.
They don't ask for an outline: their rectangle, rounded all the way, is what
makes them roll.¶
balls: 18 → [].translate(
	ƒ(number)
		Phrase(
			"⚽"
			1.1m
			name: "ball\number\"
			place: Motion(
				Place(Random(-2m 2m) ((number × 1.8m) + 44m))
				Velocity(Random(-1m/s 1m/s) 0m/s)
			)
			matter: Matter(bounciness: 0.3 friction: 0.4 roundedness: 0.5)
		)
)

Stage(
	[
		¶A floor, and two walls against the bucket's sides.¶
		Shape(Rectangle(-10m -11m 10m -12m))
		Shape(Rectangle(-8.8m 12m -7.8m -11m))
		Shape(Rectangle(7.8m 12m 8.8m -11m))
		cup
		:pile
		:hearts
		:balls
	]
	gravity: 9.8m/s^2
	place: Place(0m -1m -17m)
	background: Color(25% 20 250°)
)
